<title>BELGIUM: Belgium raises liquidity at money tender.</title>
<headline>Belgium raises liquidity at money tender.</headline>
<dateline>BRUSSELS 1997-03-28</dateline>
<text>
<p>The Belgian central bank raised money market liquidity at its fixed-rate tender for seven-day advances, which was brought forward because of Easter.</p>
<p>    Value date 02/04	  expiry on 09/04    NBVA</p>
<p>    Amount allotted	   10.000 bln bfr    ( 7.000 bln *)</p>
<p>    Interest rate	     3.00 pct	    (3.00 pct **)</p>
<p>    Total amount of bids   133.500 bln bfr</p>
<p>Percentage of bids accepted  7.35</p>
<p>* amount draining from the money market on April 2</p>
<p>** interest rate at previous tender on March 24</p>
<p>-- Brussels Newsroom +32 2 287 6810, Fax +32 2 230 7710</p>
</text>
